            "text": "Thus, when occupying a high situation he is not proud, and in a low situation he is not insubordinate. When the kingdom is well governed, he is sure by his words to rise; and when it is ill governed, he is sure by his silence to command forbearance to himself. Is not this what we find in the Book of Poetry,-\"Intelligent is he and prudent, and so preserves his person?\"",
            "translator": "Legge",
